Founded in 1892, **Liverpool Football Club** is one of the most successful and globally recognized institutions in sports history. Based at Anfield Stadium in Liverpool, England, the Reds are world-famous for their passionate fanbase, rich history, and iconic anthem, *"You'll Never Walk Alone."*

The club's rise to dominance began in the 1960s under legendary manager Bill Shankly, who built the foundation for decades of success, followed by Bob Paisley, who steered the club to European glory. Liverpool’s modern era has been equally thrilling, highlighted by the "Miracle of Istanbul" in the 2005 UEFA Champions League final and the high-energy "heavy metal football" era under Jürgen Klopp, which secured the 2019 Champions League title and the 2019–20 Premier League trophy—ending a 30-year top-flight league title drought.

---

### **Key Honors:**

* **19 English Top-Flight Titles** (First Division / Premier League)
* **6 European Cups / UEFA Champions Leagues** *(most of any English club)*
* **8 FA Cups** & **10 League Cups** (EFL Cup record holders)

---

Defined by famous rivalries with Manchester United and cross-city neighbors Everton (the Merseyside derby), Liverpool FC is far more than just a football club to its supporters. Driven by a tradition of resilience, community pride, and relentless ambition, the Reds remain an undisputed titan of world football.